<title>USA: LTV completes Varco-Pruden acquisition.</title>
<headline>LTV completes Varco-Pruden acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>LTV Corp said Wednesday that it has concluded the purchase of the assets of Varco-Pruden Buildings from United Dominion Industries Ltd for approximately $187.5 million in cash.</p>
<p>Varco-Pruden engineers and manufactures pre-engineered, non-residential, low-rise steel building systems. The purchase, said the company, also included the assets of AEP Span, a manufacturer of building system components.</p>
<p>Varco-Pruden, said the company, will operate as a subsidiary of LTV, and do business as VP Buildings Inc. It had revenues of $305 million in 1996.</p>
<p>LTV is a producer of flat rolled and tubular steel and had 1996 sales of $4.13 billion.</p>
</text>
